  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Incoming Health Mission India</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Incoming mission from India with hospitals, universities and companies to introduce Indian organisations to the Dutch life sciences and health sector, inspire them with Dutch successes and facilitate knowledge exchange and cooperation between the Netherlands and India. This incoming mission is part of several activities organised under the Indo-Dutch living lab, which provides a bilateral platform between the Netherlands and India connecting companies, public organisations and higher education institutions from both countries &#x2013; to develop and apply practical solutions for the real-life societal challenges in both countries by providing state of the art applied research and real-life practical assignments for students, lecturers, researchers and professionals from the field. India has to deal with several healthcare challenges, and lifestyle-related diseases are on the rise, with increasing numbers of cancer, diabetes and cardiovascular diseases. The government has developed plans to address the negative healthcare trends by improving health insurance coverage, expanding primary healthcare, and increasing public spending on healthcare. Given the challenges faced by the country, along with an increase in spending and a rapidly growing middle class, India offers an intriguing market to explore for innovative Dutch products, services, and technology.In 2017, two Living Lab workshops were organised. The first introductory session was held on June 20th 2017, followed by a workshop on October 24th 2017, both in Bangalore. The theme for the Living Lab is &#x201c;access to affordable healthcare via means of e-health&#x201d;, with three sub-themes: E-health, Chronic Diseases, Mental Health and Elderly Care.</narrative>
  </description>
